# Request: the name of the frame to fly to.
#
# Accepts either:
#   - a detected target frame, e.g. "target_aruco_7"
#     (resolved from the averaged map-frame estimate built by
#      detection_callback, NOT by a live TF lookup - target_* frames
#      only exist in TF while the marker is actually in view)
#   - any frame that is genuinely in the TF tree, e.g. "home"
string frame
---
# Response: whether the request was accepted onto the queue.
# NOTE: success=True means "queued", not "flight complete". The
# flight itself happens on the main thread afterwards.
bool success
string message